// Modified:   06.03.2024 Rev1
//
// Description: Tests the MLPRO2 Flood Array-Back PCB
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box above.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: PCB266-020-025.png
CLICK_OK:

#2: Setup equipment 1
a. Set adjustable PSU output 1 to 12V ±0.1V, 1.5A ±0.1A and switch the output off.
b. Using TE159, connect the PSU to the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
c. Connect the PC (via USB3 Cable Type B) to K5 the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
d. Connect the USB cable from the TE086 (LED Test Box with Web Camera) to the PC. 
COMMENT: *Example image below*
DISPLAY: TE192Setup.jpg
CLICK_OK:

#3: Setup equipment 2
a. Using the ribbon cable(TE006) connect the Test Box (TE192) at PL6 to PL2 on the ML-PRO Flood Back PCB.  
b. Connect the Test Oblique PCB (TE068) to CONN1 on the ML-PRO Flood Back PCB (266-025). 
c. Set SW1 on the ML-PRO Flood Back PCB (266-025) to the address to position 1.
d. Fit the PCB to the ML PRO PCB Fixture 1 (TE190) and connect the test PCB (TE068).
e. Place the PCB inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
f. Switch the output of the adjustable PSU on and power on the ML PRO 2 Controller Test Box (TE192).
DISPLAY: ObliqueSetup3.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: MLPRO2 
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #2

#4: PCB communication check
COMMAND: MLPRO2  BENUM
READLINE: MLPRO2  BENUM
IF:
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = BL1,BL2

Returned result is = %BENUM%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . sorry
PASS_FAIL: #4
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat


#5: RED LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2  FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 100000 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #5

#6: GREEN LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 010000 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #6

#7: BLUEGREEN LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 001000 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #7

#8: BLUE LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000100 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #8

#9: VIOLET LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000010 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #9

#10: UV LED Test
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
IMPORTANT: You may see light reflections
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 4095
DELAY: 100
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000001 4095
DELAY: 2000
PASS_FAIL: #10

#11: White LED test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000001 0
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEWHITE 1024
a. View the windows camera feed and check for 2 LED hot spots.
PASS_FAIL: #11
COMMAND: MLPRO2 SIDEWHITE 0

#12: All off LED Test
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 0
Check all lights are off and click OK.
CLICK_OK:

#13: Test complete:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and then power off the PSU and disconnect the PCB.
IMPORTANT: Check operator intials and serial number have been enterd.
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
COMMAND: MLPRO2 FLOOD 000000 0
DISCONNECT: MLPRO2
// End of file
